   "description": "The Rolex Submariner Date reference 126610LN entered production in September 2020 and remains in the current catalog. This reference is significant for introducing the 41mm case architecture, which features slimmer, more tapered lugs compared to its \"super case\" predecessor, and an increased lug width of 21mm. It houses the caliber 3235 movement, incorporating the Chronergy escapement and providing a 70-hour power reserve. The dial is black lacquer with a Cerachrom ceramic bezel insert and Chromalight luminescence. Collectors prioritize this model for its modernized proportions that more closely resemble vintage aesthetics while utilizing current mechanical technology. On the secondary market, prices typically range from $13,000 to $16,000 depending on condition and documentation. A notable production detail is the inclusion of a small Rolex crown emblem between \"Swiss\" and \"Made\" at the six o'clock position, signifying the updated movement generation."
